<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PathAssistant xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- DEACTIVATED 2026-08-09 (Tranche 3C), NOT DELETED, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.

         Contract_Review__c gained two record types in this tranche (Acquisition_PSA,
         Disposition_PSA). A Path is configured PER RECORD TYPE, and recordTypeName CANNOT BE
         RE-POINTED on an existing PathAssistant - so this __MASTER__ path is superseded by two
         new files, Contract_Review_Path_Acquisition and Contract_Review_Path_Disposition,
         exactly as Tranche 2 superseded Disposition_Path, 3A superseded NDA_Path and 3B
         superseded LOI_Path.

         It is retained rather than deleted because it is the record of the guidance text the
         ACQUISITION steps were copied from. Contract_Review_Path_Acquisition carries all four
         <info> texts BYTE-IDENTICAL to the steps below - including the `&amp;amp;amp;` in the first
         one - and like this file it declares no <fieldNames> on any step; that absence was
         copied forward too rather than being "improved".

         Once record types exist, a __MASTER__ path renders for the Master type only - which
         after the row migration is NO ROWS. Leaving it active would do nothing useful and would
         make the Path configuration ambiguous to the next reader.

         ORDER OF OPERATIONS AT DEPLOY: profile record-type assignment and the migration of every
         existing Contract Review row off Master onto Acquisition_PSA must both complete BEFORE
         the two new paths are relied on - a row still on Master matches no record-type Path and
         renders a Path with no current position. Same gate as Tranche 2's A2.

         Everything below this line is the ORIGINAL note and remains accurate about the field
         choice, which both successor files inherit unchanged.
         ====================================================================================
         ⚠ DRIVEN BY Negotiation_Status__c, NOT Stage__c. Replaces Contract_Review_Path (now
         inactive), which could not simply be re-pointed: the Metadata API refuses to change
         fieldName on an existing PathAssistant.

         Stage__c is a DERIVED PROJECTION here — the before-save flow Contract_Review_Stage_Sync
         recomputes it from Negotiation_Status__c on every save — so a Path on Stage__c could not
         match the workflow. Two of the three original mismatches are now gone because the counter
         values were removed outright (below); the one that made a Stage__c Path unworkable remains:
         'Revised' and 'Ready for Execution' BOTH project to 'Review', so a Stage__c Path would sit
         still through one of the Advance Stage clicks.

         On Negotiation_Status__c the Path and the Advance Stage button are the SAME sequence:
         every click moves exactly one step and nothing is advertised that never happens.

         ⚠ STEP ORDER COMES FROM THE PICKLIST, NOT FROM THIS FILE. The retired Path listed its steps
         alphabetically yet rendered in picklist order, so do not infer display order from the order
         below. Negotiation_Status__c is ordered Initial Draft, Revised, Ready for Execution,
         Executed — which is exactly the intended line, so every value is a step and none is skipped.

         ⚠ SELLER COUNTER / BUYER COUNTER NO LONGER EXIST (removed 2026-08-05). Redlines are recorded
         as PSA_Version__c rows plus Ball_In_Court__c, not as a status, so a negotiating record now
         sits on 'Revised' instead of dropping off the Path — which is why this step's coaching text
         tells the user to stay here and keep logging versions. Do not reintroduce a counter status
         without also revisiting PsaVersionService, which deliberately no longer writes this field. -->
    <active>false</active>
    <entityName>Contract_Review__c</entityName>
    <fieldName>Negotiation_Status__c</fieldName>
    <masterLabel>Contract Review Negotiation Path</masterLabel>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>Draft the purchase &amp;amp; sale agreement from the agreed LOI terms. Circulate the first draft and capture the PSA date.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Initial Draft</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>Review the PSA internally. Validate terms, contingencies and timelines. Redlines happen here: log every exchange with Log Version — each one records who sent it and flips Ball In Court — and stay on this step for as long as the negotiation runs. Advance only once the document is final.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Revised</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>Terms are locked and the document is final. Route for signature. Advancing from here executes the contract, so confirm every contingency and date is agreed first.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Ready for Execution</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>PSA fully executed — this hands the deal off to the Transactions team: the Opportunity is stamped Contract Signed (Day 0) and the Transaction record is created automatically. The execution date is stamped for you.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Executed</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <recordTypeName>__MASTER__</recordTypeName>
</PathAssistant>
